# Backlog 64 (fixed 0.4): a `pin` must not delete a drawing. Until
# 0.4 the self-edge route was gated on "neither endpoint is pinned" —
# a guard that belongs to the CHANNEL route, whose lane plan is an auto-layout
# artefact — so a pinned node's self-edge fell through to the straight route
# and drew a ZERO-LENGTH line at the node's own centre, with the edge label
# printed across the node's name. No error, no warning, a silently missing
# arc. The rule the fix keeps: a self-edge draws the same way whether its
# node's coordinate came from a pin or from the layout pass.
#
# The MODEL is unchanged by any of that — this fixture's golden pins the
# parse, and the DRAWING is asserted by tools/shape-check.js, which measures
# every self-loop's path length and its label's clearance off the rendered SVG.
figdown 0.1 block
title "A pinned node still draws its self-edge as a side loop"
node a "A"
node b "B"
pin a at=(0,0) width=120 height=60
pin b at=(240,0) width=120 height=60
edge a -[to b]-> b
edge a -[stay in A]-> a
edge b -[stay in B]-> b
